@startuml turns
!include theme.iuml
title Crafty — turn ownership within each isolated agent session
top to bottom direction

state "Accepted\nmessage + durable dispatch record" as Accepted
state "Dispatching\nper-agent-session ownership acquired" as Dispatching
state "Running\none active session/prompt" as Running
state "Waiting for protocol permission" as Permission
state "Cancel requested" as Cancelling #FFF3CD
state "Completed\nrecord actual stop reason" as Completed #E8F3EC
state "Cancelled" as Cancelled #FCE9E7
state "Failed" as Failed #FCE9E7
state "Interrupted / delivery uncertain" as Interrupted #FFF3CD
state "Recovering session runtime\nsame mounts + ACP session; new generation" as Recovering

[*] --> Accepted
Accepted --> Dispatching : dispatch command claimed once
Dispatching --> Running : request sent; no concurrent prompt
Running --> Permission : session/request_permission
Permission --> Running : validated response on original request ID
Running --> Completed : original prompt response
Permission --> Cancelling : Stop
Running --> Cancelling : Stop
Cancelling --> Cancelled : original prompt response = cancelled
Cancelling --> Completed : completion already won the race
Running --> Failed : terminal RPC / adapter error
Dispatching --> Interrupted : crash before delivery is known
Running --> Interrupted : runtime lost
Cancelling --> Interrupted : cancellation deadline exceeded
Permission --> Interrupted : connection lost
Interrupted --> Recovering : fence old generation; confirm old container stopped
Recovering --> [*] : resume/load if supported; release slot\nrequire explicit next message
Completed --> [*]
Cancelled --> [*]
Failed --> [*]

note right of Permission
  Protocol permission is separate from design approval.
  Ordinary photo/measurement forms are durable interactions;
  their MCP request returns without waiting for a browser.
end note
note right of Cancelling
  Cancel is a notification, not a request/response pair.
  Resolve pending permissions as cancelled.
  Request cancellation of associated CAD jobs separately.
  Stop on a work request also cancels its delegated CAD task.
  Accept final updates but fence domain publication.
end note
note right of Interrupted
  Never silently resend a prompt after an ambiguous send.
  Runtime epoch rejects events from replaced processes.
  Preserve workspace and Codex-state volumes on stop.
  Persist user messages independently of agent echoes.
end note
note bottom of Recovering
  Browser disconnect only detaches a subscriber; work continues.
  API replay uses durable sequence numbers, not timer-based "settling".
  Session load replay is reconciled separately from live events.
  Optional queued user messages are dispatched serially after a terminal turn.
  Parent and CAD sessions each have their own prompt slot and recovery state.
  Deliver child results once at a permitted parent turn boundary.
end note
@enduml
